ural casings are made from animal intestines or skin; artificial casings, introduced in the early 20th century, are made of collagen and cellulose. The material is then shaped via a continuous extrusion process—producing a single sausage casing of indefinite length—which is then cut into desired lengths, usually while the extrusion process continues."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sausage-casing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sausage_casing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine",[["Haggis","dish/haggis"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Oatmeal","ingredient/oatmeal"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Suet","ingredient/suet"]]}]},"dish/jiaozi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/jiaozi","n":"Jiaozi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Jiaozi are a type of Chinese dumpling. They typically consist of a ground meat or vegetable filling wrapped into a thinly rolled piece of dough, which is then sealed by pressing the edges together. They can be boiled (水饺; 水餃; shuǐjiǎo), steamed (蒸饺; 蒸餃; zhēngjiǎo), pan-fried (煎饺; 煎餃; jiānjiǎo), deep-fried (炸饺; 炸餃; zhájiǎo, zhàjiǎo), or baked (烤饺; 烤餃; kǎojiǎo), and are traditionally served with a black vinegar and soy sauce dip. They can also be served in a soup (汤饺; 湯餃; tāngjiǎo). Jiaozi have great cultural significance within China. They are one of the major dishes eaten during the Chinese New Year throughout northern China and eaten all year round in the northern provinces. Their resemblance to the gold and silver ingots (sycee) used in Imperial China has meant that they symbolize wealth and good fortune."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-jiaozi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiaozi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["A+ Hong Kong Kitchen","dish/a-hong-kong-kitchen"],["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Chinese Tuxedo","dish/chinese-tuxedo"],["Chowking","dish/chowking"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Country Dough","dish/country-dough"],["Cuisine AuntDai","dish/cuisine-auntdai"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dim Sum King","dish/dim-sum-king"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Duck House Chinese Restaurant","dish/duck-house-chinese-restaurant"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Flower Drum